{"id":"mahabharata-13-058","work":"mahabharata","part":13,"partName":"अनुशासनपर्व","partNameEn":"Anushasana Parva","unit":58,"title":"अष्टपञ्चाशत्तमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 58 · The best gifts","summary":{"en":"Yudhishthira asks which gift is the best of the gifts given outside the sacrificial altar. Bhishma says that one should guard against brahmins who are like venomous snakes and bow to those who live rightly, and that he himself does not grieve at what he gave to brahmins.","kn":"ವೇದಿಯ ಹೊರಗೆ ನೀಡುವ ದಾನಗಳಲ್ಲಿ ಯಾವುದು ಶ್ರೇಷ್ಠವೆಂದು ಯುಧಿಷ್ಠಿರ ಕೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ. ವಿಷಸರ್ಪದಂತಹ ಬ್ರಾಹ್ಮಣರಿಂದ ಎಚ್ಚರದಿಂದಿರಬೇಕು, ಸರಿಯಾಗಿ ಬದುಕುವವರಿಗೆ ನಮಿಸಬೇಕು, ತಾನು ಬ್ರಾಹ್ಮಣರಿಗೆ ಮಾಡಿದುದರ ಬಗ್ಗೆ ಪಶ್ಚಾತ್ತಾಪವಿಲ್ಲ ಎಂದು ಭೀಷ್ಮ ಹೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"युधिष्ठिर पूछते हैं कि वेदी के बाहर दिए जाने वाले दानों में कौन-सा श्रेष्ठ है। भीष्म कहते हैं कि विषैले सर्प जैसे ब्राह्मणों से बचना और सही जीवन जीने वालों को नमन करना चाहिए, और उन्हें ब्राह्मणों को दिए पर पछतावा नहीं।","te":"వేదికి వెలుపల ఇచ్చే దానాలలో ఏది శ్రేష్ఠమని యుధిష్ఠిరుడు అడుగుతాడు. విషసర్పాల వంటి బ్రాహ్మణుల నుండి జాగ్రత్తగా ఉండాలని, సరిగ్గా జీవించేవారికి నమస్కరించాలని, తాను బ్రాహ్మణులకు చేసినదానికి పశ్చాత్తాపపడనని భీష్ముడు అంటాడు.","ta":"வேதிக்கு வெளியே தரும் தானங்களில் எது சிறந்தது என்று யுதிஷ்டிரர் கேட்க, நஞ்சுப் பாம்பு போன்ற அந்தணரிடம் எச்சரிக்கை, முறையாக வாழ்வோரை வணங்க வேண்டும், தாம் அந்தணருக்குச் செய்ததற்கு வருந்தவில்லை என்று பீஷ்மர் கூறுகிறார்.","ml":"യാഗവേദിക്ക് പുറത്തുള്ള ദാനങ്ങളിൽ ഏതു ദാനമാണ് ഏറ്റവും ശ്രേഷ്ഠമെന്ന് യുധിഷ്ഠിരൻ ചോദിക്കുന്നു. വിഷമുള്ള പാമ്പുകളെപ്പോലുള്ള ബ്രാഹ്മണരിൽനിന്ന് ജാഗ്രത പാലിക്കണമെന്നും, ശരിയായി ജീവിക്കുന്നവരെ വണങ്ങണമെന്നും ഭീഷ്മർ പറയുന്നു; ബ്രാഹ്മണർക്ക് നൽകിയതിനെക്കുറിച്ച് താൻ ദുഃഖിക്കുന്നില്ലെന്നും അദ്ദേഹം പറയുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 13.58; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Tue Nov 03 2026","sections":[{"title":"आनुशासनिकपर्व","titleEn":"Anushasanika Parva (The instructions)","verses":[{"text":"युधिष्ठिर उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Yudhishthira said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"यानीमानि बहिर्वेद्यां दानानि परिचक्षते ।\nतेभ्यो विशिष्टं किं दानं मतं ते कुरुपुंगव ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Among these gifts that are spoken of as made outside the sacrificial altar, which gift do you consider the best, tiger of the Kurus?"}},{"n":2,"text":"कौतूहलं हि परमं तत्र मे वर्तते प्रभो ।\nदातारं दत्तमन्वेति यद्दानं तत्प्रचक्ष्व मे ॥","meaning":{"en":"I have great curiosity about it, lord; tell me which gift follows the giver.\""}},{"text":"भीष्म उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Bhishma said:"}},{"n":3,"text":"अभयं सर्वभूतेभ्यो व्यसने चाप्यनुग्रहम् ।\nयच्चाभिलषितं दद्यात्तृषितायाभियाचते ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Safety for all creatures, kindness in distress, and giving what a thirsty beggar desires,"}},{"n":4,"text":"दत्तं मन्येत यद्दत्त्वा तद्दानं श्रेष्ठमुच्यते ।\nदत्तं दातारमन्वेति यद्दानं भरतर्षभ ॥","meaning":{"en":"a gift that the giver feels is truly given: that gift is called the best, the gift that follows the giver, best of Bharatas."}},{"n":5,"text":"हिरण्यदानं गोदानं पृथिवीदानमेव च ।\nएतानि वै पवित्राणि तारयन्त्यपि दुष्कृतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Gifts of gold, cows and land are purifying, and they carry even the sinner across."}},{"n":6,"text":"एतानि पुरुषव्याघ्र साधुभ्यो देहि नित्यदा ।\nदानानि हि नरं पापान्मोक्षयन्ति न संशयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Give these constantly to good people, tiger among men; gifts free a man from sin, without doubt."}},{"n":7,"text":"यद्यदिष्टतमं लोके यच्चास्य दयितं गृहे ।\nतत्तद्गुणवते देयं तदेवाक्षयमिच्छता ॥","meaning":{"en":"Whatever is dearest in the world and whatever is cherished in his house, that should be given to a worthy person by one who wants it to be imperishable."}},{"n":8,"text":"प्रियाणि लभते लोके प्रियदः प्रियकृत्तथा ।\nप्रियो भवति भूतानामिह चैव परत्र च ॥","meaning":{"en":"One who gives what is dear, and does what is dear, gains what is dear in the world; he becomes dear to beings here and hereafter."}},{"n":9,"text":"याचमानमभीमानादाशावन्तमकिंचनम् ।\nयो नार्चति यथाशक्ति स नृशंसो युधिष्ठिर ॥","meaning":{"en":"One who does not honour, as best he can, a hopeful, humble beggar without possessions is cruel, Yudhishthira."}},{"n":10,"text":"अमित्रमपि चेद्दीनं शरणैषिणमागतम् ।\nव्यसने योऽनुगृह्णाति स वै पुरुषसत्तमः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Even if an enemy comes in distress seeking refuge, the one who helps him in his misfortune is the best of men."}},{"n":11,"text":"कृशाय ह्रीमते तात वृत्तिक्षीणाय सीदते ।\nअपहन्यात्क्षुधं यस्तु न तेन पुरुषः समः ॥","meaning":{"en":"One who removes the hunger of a thin, modest person ruined in livelihood and sinking is not equal to other men."}},{"n":12,"text":"ह्रिया तु नियतान्साधून्पुत्रदारैश्च कर्शितान् ।\nअयाचमानान्कौन्तेय सर्वोपायैर्निमन्त्रय ॥","meaning":{"en":"Invite, by every means, Kaunteya, the good who are restrained by modesty, weakened by wife and children, and who do not beg."}},{"n":13,"text":"आशिषं ये न देवेषु न मर्त्येषु च कुर्वते ।\nअर्हन्तो नित्यसत्त्वस्था यथालब्धोपजीविनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those worthy ones who offer no blessing to gods or to mortals, ever steadfast, living on whatever they get,"}},{"n":14,"text":"आशीविषसमेभ्यश्च तेभ्यो रक्षस्व भारत ।\nतान्युक्तैरुपजिज्ञास्य तथा द्विजवरोत्तमान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"protect against them as if from poisonous snakes, Bharata; and learning of them through trusted people, also the best of the brahmins."}},{"n":15,"text":"कृतैरावसथैर्नित्यं सप्रेष्यैः सपरिच्छदैः ।\nनिमन्त्रयेथाः कौरव्य सर्वकामसुखावहैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Invite them, Kaurava, to dwellings you have built, with attendants and furnishings, giving every desired comfort."}},{"n":16,"text":"यदि ते प्रतिगृह्णीयुः श्रद्धापूतं युधिष्ठिर ।\nकार्यमित्येव मन्वाना धार्मिकाः पुण्यकर्मिणः ॥","meaning":{"en":"If those righteous and virtuous ones accept what is purified by faith, Yudhishthira, thinking it a duty,"}},{"n":17,"text":"विद्यास्नाता व्रतस्नाता ये व्यपाश्रित्यजीविनः ।\nगूढस्वाध्यायतपसो ब्राह्मणाः संशितव्रताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"those brahmins who are graduates of learning and of vows, who depend on no one, who keep their study and austerity hidden, and whose vows are sharp,"}},{"n":18,"text":"तेषु शुद्धेषु दान्तेषु स्वदारनिरतेषु च ।\nयत्करिष्यसि कल्याणं तत्त्वा लोकेषु धास्यति ॥","meaning":{"en":"whatever good you do for those pure, self-controlled ones devoted to their own wives will support you in the worlds."}},{"n":19,"text":"यथाग्निहोत्रं सुहुतं सायं प्रातर्द्विजातिना ।\nतथा भवति दत्तं वै द्विजेभ्योऽथ कृतात्मना ॥","meaning":{"en":"As an offering into the fire well made morning and evening by a twice-born, so is a gift to brahmins by one of controlled self."}},{"n":20,"text":"एष ते विततो यज्ञः श्रद्धापूतः सदक्षिणः ।\nविशिष्टः सर्वयज्ञेभ्यो ददतस्तात वर्तताम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"This is your sacrifice spread out, purified by faith and with fees, better than all sacrifices, for one who gives, dear one."}},{"n":21,"text":"निवापो दानसदृशस्तादृशेषु युधिष्ठिर ।\nनिवपन्पूजयंश्चैव तेष्वानृण्यं निगच्छति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Offering to such people is equal to a gift, Yudhishthira; offering and honouring them, one is freed from debt toward them."}},{"n":22,"text":"य एव नो न कुप्यन्ति न लुभ्यन्ति तृणेष्वपि ।\nत एव नः पूज्यतमा ये चान्ये प्रियवादिनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those who do not get angry with us and are not greedy even for a blade of grass, and others who speak kindly, are the most to be honoured by us."}},{"n":23,"text":"ये नो न बहु मन्यन्ते न प्रवर्तन्ति चापरे ।\nपुत्रवत्परिपाल्यास्ते नमस्तेभ्यस्तथाभयम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those who do not think much of us and do not act on our behalf should be protected like sons; reverence to them, and safety."}},{"n":24,"text":"ऋत्विक्पुरोहिताचार्या मृदुब्रह्मधरा हि ते ।\nक्षत्रेणापि हि संसृष्टं तेजः शाम्यति वै द्विजे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Priests, family priests and teachers bear the soft power of Brahma; for even the splendour of a kshatriya joined with it is calmed in a brahmin."}},{"n":25,"text":"अस्ति मे बलवानस्मि राजास्मीति युधिष्ठिर ।\nब्राह्मणान्मा स्म पर्यश्नीर्वासोभिरशनेन च ॥","meaning":{"en":"Do not, Yudhishthira, think 'I have wealth, I am strong, I am king,' and cheat brahmins of clothing and food."}},{"n":26,"text":"यच्छोभार्थं बलार्थं वा वित्तमस्ति तवानघ ।\nतेन ते ब्राह्मणाः पूज्याः स्वधर्ममनुतिष्ठता ॥","meaning":{"en":"With whatever wealth you have for show or for strength, blameless one, you should honour brahmins while following your own duty."}},{"n":27,"text":"नमस्कार्यास्त्वया विप्रा वर्तमाना यथातथम् ।\nयथासुखं यथोत्साहं ललन्तु त्वयि पुत्रवत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Brahmins as they are should be saluted by you; let them dote on you like a son, at their ease and with enthusiasm."}},{"n":28,"text":"को ह्यन्यः सुप्रसादानां सुहृदामल्पतोषिणाम् ।\nवृत्तिमर्हत्युपक्षेप्तुं त्वदन्यः कुरुसत्तम ॥","meaning":{"en":"Who else but you, best of the Kurus, deserves to bestow a livelihood on those who are gracious and satisfied with little?"}},{"n":29,"text":"यथा पत्याश्रयो धर्मः स्त्रीणां लोके सनातनः ।\nस देवः सा गतिर्नान्या तथास्माकं द्विजातयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"As a husband is the eternal refuge of wives in this world, he is their god and their only path, so the twice-born are for us."}},{"n":30,"text":"यदि नो ब्राह्मणास्तात संत्यजेयुरपूजिताः ।\nपश्यन्तो दारुणं कर्म सततं क्षत्रिये स्थितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"If the brahmins, unhonoured, were to abandon us, seeing the cruel deeds ever present in a kshatriya,"}},{"n":31,"text":"अवेदानामकीर्तीनामलोकानामयज्वनाम् ।\nकोऽस्माकं जीवितेनार्थस्तद्धि नो ब्राह्मणाश्रयम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"what use would our lives be, without Vedas, without fame, without worlds, without sacrifices? For our existence depends on brahmins."}},{"n":32,"text":"अत्र ते वर्तयिष्यामि यथा धर्मः सनातनः ।\nराजन्यो ब्राह्मणं राजन्पुरा परिचचार ह ।\nवैश्यो राजन्यमित्येव शूद्रो वैश्यमिति श्रुतिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Here I will tell you how the eternal dharma stands. In ancient times a kshatriya served a brahmin, a vaishya a kshatriya, and a shudra a vaishya; so the tradition says."}},{"n":33,"text":"दूराच्छूद्रेणोपचर्यो ब्राह्मणोऽग्निरिव ज्वलन् ।\nसंस्पर्शपरिचर्यस्तु वैश्येन क्षत्रियेण च ॥","meaning":{"en":"A brahmin, blazing like fire, should be served from afar by a shudra; but a vaishya and a kshatriya may serve him by touch."}},{"n":34,"text":"मृदुभावान्सत्यशीलान्सत्यधर्मानुपालकान् ।\nआशीविषानिव क्रुद्धांस्तानुपाचरत द्विजान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Serve those brahmins who are gentle, truthful and keepers of truth and dharma, though when angry they are like poisonous snakes."}},{"n":35,"text":"अपरेषां परेषां च परेभ्यश्चैव ये परे ।\nक्षत्रियाणां प्रतपतां तेजसा च बलेन च ।\nब्राह्मणेष्वेव शाम्यन्ति तेजांसि च तपांसि च ॥","meaning":{"en":"For the kshatriyas, blazing with splendour and strength, for those who come after others, and for those beyond them, all splendours and austerities are calmed in brahmins alone."}},{"n":36,"text":"न मे पिता प्रियतरो न त्वं तात तथा प्रियः ।\nन मे पितुः पिता राजन्न चात्मा न च जीवितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"My father is not dearer to me, nor are you, dear one, nor my father's father, nor my own self, nor my life."}},{"n":37,"text":"त्वत्तश्च मे प्रियतरः पृथिव्यां नास्ति कश्चन ।\nत्वत्तोऽपि मे प्रियतरा ब्राह्मणा भरतर्षभ ॥","meaning":{"en":"There is no one on earth dearer to me than you; yet brahmins are dearer to me than you, best of Bharatas."}},{"n":38,"text":"ब्रवीमि सत्यमेतच्च यथाहं पाण्डुनन्दन ।\nतेन सत्येन गच्छेयं लोकान्यत्र स शंतनुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"I speak this truth, son of Pandu; by that truth may I go to the worlds where Shantanu is."}},{"n":39,"text":"पश्येयं च सतां लोकाञ्छुचीन्ब्रह्मपुरस्कृतान् ।\nतत्र मे तात गन्तव्यमह्नाय च चिराय च ॥","meaning":{"en":"And may I see the pure worlds of the good, with brahmins at their head; there I must go, sooner or later."}},{"n":40,"text":"सोऽहमेतादृशाँल्लोकान्दृष्ट्वा भरतसत्तम ।\nयन्मे कृतं ब्राह्मणेषु न तप्ये तेन पार्थिव ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having seen such worlds, best of Bharatas, I do not grieve, king, over what I have done to brahmins.\""}}]}]}